<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">International Monetary Fund</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as IMF</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The International Monetary Fund (IMF) is an international financial institution founded in 1944 to support monetary co-operation and provide emergency financing. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-crisis">Suez Crisis</a> of 1956, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> threatened to block IMF support for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> unless it withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. Britain's retreat showed it could no longer act independently, a milestone in the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/international-monetary-fund.jpg" alt="International Monetary Fund" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US Dept of Treasury. Note that while the IMF is independent, at its creation in 1945 it asked the US DoT to create the logo. … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IMF-Seal_ENG_RGB.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
